\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 ReapeZoom\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Turning long Zoom-recorder captures into finished material, two ways.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Split rehearsal recording into song regions} \u8212- one long rehearsal becomes named regions, one per song, ready to render at streaming loudness. It does not split on silence: between songs a rehearsal is full of talking, tuning and noodling. It finds quiet gaps of a minimum length, then discards spans too short to be a song.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Split percussion recording into hits} \u8212- a pass-per-sound-type recording becomes one track per sound type, one item per hit.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Build sampler preset from tracks} \u8212- measures every hit, sorts it into velocity layers and round robins, lays the matrix out on the arrange grid for review, and writes both {\f1 \fs24 .sfz} and {\f1 \fs24 .dspreset}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Thresholds are relative to the material's own peak, so they work on quiet 32-bit-float captures without recalibration.\par}
}
